<SousbookInfo title="Support" description="Get help with Sousbook recipes, purchases, imports and iCloud.">

<p>Need help saving a recipe, restoring Pro, importing a photo or using cooking mode? Contact RandyVentures and include your device model, iOS version, Sousbook version and what happened.</p>
<p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:randyventures06@gmail.com?subject=Sousbook%20support">randyventures06@gmail.com</a><br /><strong>Phone:</strong> <a href="tel:+19565306901">+1 956-530-6901</a></p>
<p>Include any error message and a screenshot if useful. Please remove passwords, payment information and sensitive personal details. Support is for the app and does not provide emergency, medical or individualized allergy advice.</p>
<h2>Restore a purchase</h2>
<p>Use the Apple account that made the purchase, then choose <strong>Restore purchases</strong> on the paywall or in Settings. A working internet connection may be needed. If access still does not return, contact support with the plan name and error message. Do not send your Apple account password.</p>
<h2>Manage a subscription or request a refund</h2>
<p>Open <a href="https://apps.apple.com/account/subscriptions">Apple's subscription settings</a> to manage or cancel the annual plan. Deleting Sousbook does not cancel it. Lifetime is a one-time purchase without recurring billing. Refund requests can be made through <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com/">Apple's Report a Problem page</a>.</p>
<h2>Check an imported recipe</h2>
<p>Some websites cannot be imported automatically. Try pasting the recipe text or scanning a clear, well-lit copy you have permission to use. Check imported ingredients, quantities, temperatures and steps against the original before cooking. Read the <a href="/sousbook/food-safety/">food safety guidance</a>.</p>
<h2>Recipes, iCloud and backups</h2>
<p>Your cookbook is stored on your device. Private iCloud sync depends on your Apple account, available storage, connectivity and supported app configuration. The iCloud row in Settings reports account availability; it does not confirm every change has synced. Keep independent copies of important recipes. If data seems missing, contact support before deleting the app or clearing iCloud storage.</p>
<h2>Cooking timers</h2>
<p>Allow notifications in iOS Settings if you want alerts outside the app. Focus modes and notification settings can affect delivery. Timers do not verify doneness: use a food thermometer and current food-safety guidance.</p>
<h2>Privacy requests</h2>
<p>Email support with “Sousbook privacy” in the subject. See the <a href="/sousbook/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> for what the app processes, retention limits and deletion options.</p>

</SousbookInfo>
